23
00:00:58,111 --> 00:01:00,823
to target different places in the DOM.

24
00:01:01,786 --> 00:01:04,787
So instead of returning just one fragment or

25
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,932
one HTML structure, which then is

26
00:01:08,509 --> 00:01:12,280
used to swap some part of the website that

27
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:15,008
is defined with help of hx-target and

28
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:15,907
hx-swap,

29
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:19,165
instead of just doing that, you can use this

30
00:01:19,421 --> 00:01:22,662
out-of-band swap functionality to return

31
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:25,437
multiple fragments for multiple targets.

32
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,956
And here's how that works.

33
00:01:28,886 --> 00:01:31,004
Let's start in that POST route here.

